=== Timestamp form — default step = INTERVAL 1 DAY ===
SELECT * FROM GENERATE_SERIES(TIMESTAMP '2024-01-01', TIMESTAMP '2024-01-04');
ERROR 1064: You have an error in your SQL syntax; check the manual that corresponds to your MySQL server version for the right syntax to use near '(TIMESTAMP '2024-01-01', TIMESTAMP '2024-01-04')' at line 1
=== Timestamp form — custom INTERVAL step ===
SELECT * FROM GENERATE_SERIES(TIMESTAMP '2024-01-01',
                              TIMESTAMP '2024-01-10',
                              INTERVAL 3 DAY);
ERROR 1064: You have an error in your SQL syntax; check the manual that corresponds to your MySQL server version for the right syntax to use near '(TIMESTAMP '2024-01-01',
                              TIMESTAMP '2024-01-10',
 ' at line 1
SELECT * FROM GENERATE_SERIES(TIMESTAMP '2024-01-01 00:00:00',
                              TIMESTAMP '2024-01-01 06:00:00',
                              INTERVAL 2 HOUR);
ERROR 1064: You have an error in your SQL syntax; check the manual that corresponds to your MySQL server version for the right syntax to use near '(TIMESTAMP '2024-01-01 00:00:00',
                              TIMESTAMP '2024-' at line 1
